# The corpus is a fixture, not a working tree. Every file under corpus/ is
# checked in on purpose, including the ones that are machine exhaust anywhere
# else.
#
# A global gitignore commonly carries `**/.claude/settings.local.json`, which
# would silently drop one file from a 43-file corpus whose counts the suite
# asserts. A .gitignore this deep outranks core.excludesFile, so the negation
# here is what actually keeps the file.
!corpus/**/settings.local.json
